𝗞𝘂𝗯𝗲𝗿𝗻𝗲𝘁𝗲𝘀 𝗗𝗮𝗲𝗺𝗼𝗻𝗦𝗲𝘁 – 𝗢𝗻𝗲 𝗣𝗼𝗱 𝘁𝗼 𝗥𝘂𝗹𝗲 𝗘𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘆 𝗡𝗼𝗱𝗲!

Ever needed to run the same pod on every node in your Kubernetes cluster? That’s exactly what a DaemonSet is made for!

🔹 𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗶𝘀 𝗮 𝗗𝗮𝗲𝗺𝗼𝗻𝗦𝗲𝘁?
A DaemonSet ensures that a copy of a pod runs on all (or selected) nodes in the cluster. It automatically handles pod placement as nodes are added or removed.

🛠️ 𝗨𝘀𝗲 𝗖𝗮𝘀𝗲𝘀:
✅ Log collectors (e.g., Fluentd, Filebeat)
✅ Monitoring agents (e.g., Prometheus Node Exporter)
✅ Security agents and node-level tools
✅ Custom storage daemons or network plugins

🔐 𝗪𝗵𝘆 𝗨𝘀𝗲 𝗗𝗮𝗲𝗺𝗼𝗻𝗦𝗲𝘁𝘀?
✔️ Ensures critical services are running on every node
✔️ Simplifies observability, security, and compliance setups
✔️ Supports node selectors, taints, tolerations, and affinities for fine-tuned control

🚀 𝗣𝗿𝗼 𝗧𝗶𝗽𝘀:
✔️ Use 𝘵𝘰𝘭𝘦𝘳𝘢𝘵𝘪𝘰𝘯𝘴 and 𝘯𝘰𝘥𝘦𝘚𝘦𝘭𝘦𝘤𝘵𝘰𝘳 to target specific node groups
✔️ Combine with 𝘙𝘰𝘭𝘭𝘪𝘯𝘨𝘜𝘱𝘥𝘢𝘵𝘦 strategy for safe updates
✔️ Don’t forget resource limits — DaemonSet pods can run on every node!

DaemonSets are the invisible backbone of robust Kubernetes clusters. From observability to security, they make sure your nodes are ready for anything. 💡
